\section{Solar Burst Detectability and Dynamic-Range Analysis}
\label{sec:detectability}

\subsection{Flux Levels of Solar Radio Events at \SI{610}{\mega\hertz}}

Solar radio emission at \SI{610}{\mega\hertz} spans more than four orders of
magnitude in flux density. Table~\ref{tab:detectability} classifies the principal
solar radio event types by their typical flux levels and evaluates the
detection significance against the simulation's sensitivity floor
($\Delta S_{\rm min}\approx\SI{0.058}{\sfu}$ for \texttt{INTEGRATION\_BINS}$=50$,
from Table~\ref{tab:snr-bins}).

\begin{table}[H]
  \centering
